{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia","id":1088272,"title":"How to talk with Gaia?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-05T07:20:34-07:00","id":1088272,"title":"How to talk with Gaia?","content":"Rage Across the Heavens describes Eshtarra as celestine of Earth. But Eshtarra is not Gaia. Gaia must be higher than celestine, above all the spirits, even Triat.<br /> Can werewolf meet Gaia? Not Gaia's servants but Gaia herself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12954-adrax","name":"Adrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T08:25:42-07:00","id":1088303,"title":"","content":"It most certainly does not describe Eshtarra as the Celestine of Earth. She's the Incarna of the Aetherial planetary Realm of Earth. Gaia is far, far above Eshtarra (the actual Celestine of the Earth remains unnamed and unspecified, but Gaia is presumably at least two spiritual rungs above her, too), and you only really meet Her avatar if She decides to talk. There's no easy solution, and no ritual to make it happen; even summoning a Celestine avatar is unlikely to result in a good outcome, and it's about as far as the rite of summoning can take you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:31:47-07:00","id":1088460,"title":"","content":"You have the same chance as an ant having a meaningful conversation with you, or with a better you. Rather with Einstein. While he is sleeping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T00:40:31-07:00","id":1088647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia#post1088272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rage Across the Heavens describes Eshtarra as celestine of Earth. But Eshtarra is not Gaia. Gaia must be higher than celestine, above all the spirits, even Triat.<br /> Can werewolf meet Gaia? Not Gaia's servants but Gaia herself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eshtarra is an Incarna of Gaia, one of many. Gaia has been described as having at least multiple Celestine Faces, like Devi The Emerald Mother and Sea... the Sea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T06:20:34-07:00","id":1088724,"title":"","content":"Can werewolves meet Gaia? No, not in any meaningful sense, anymore than a bacteria may 'meet' a human person.<br /> <br /> Can a werewolf interact with an avatar or aspect of Gaia? Sure. Be sure to make it suitably dramatic; this is the <i>most important spirit in the universe</i>, as far as the Changing Breeds are concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T12:15:43-07:00","id":1088818,"title":"","content":"Based on the Garou legends, you can, but ,you see, they are just legend.<br /> <br /> As far as I understand, even IF there is a singular entity known as Gaia, she is in a semi-permanent slumber.<br /> <br /> By the way, the big dragon-serpent of Pangea is also a Gaian incarnation. (And the one what represents her in the most complete way.- Based on End Times: Apocalypse) Check her out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T14:00:44-07:00","id":1088838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1088818#post1088818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the Garou legends, you can, but ,you see, they are just legend.<br /> <br /> As far as I understand, even IF there is a singular entity known as Gaia, she is in a semi-permanent slumber.<br /> <br /> By the way, the big dragon-serpent of Pangea is also a Gaian incarnation. (And the one what represents her in the most complete way.- Based on End Times: Apocalypse) Check her out.</div> </div> </div> </div>i'm fairly certain that the Great Serpent of Pangaea represents one of the few pre-corruption Wyrm manifestations in all of existence, rather than being a closer link to Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T14:26:28-07:00","id":1088849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1088838#post1088838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> i'm fairly certain that the Great Serpent of Pangaea represents one of the few pre-corruption Wyrm manifestations in all of existence, rather than being a closer link to Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was the general assumption until the 62nd page of the Time of Judgement - Apocalypse came. (If we accept it as cannon &amp; use the materials within.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T15:43:55-07:00","id":1088882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1088849#post1088849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that was the general assumption until the 62nd page of the Time of Judgement - Apocalypse came. (If we accept it as cannon &amp; use the materials within.)</div> </div> </div> </div>We can't really do that, honestly. The book was a toolkit of what-ifs, capped off with a very much out of left field presentation of what happened to Luna when the moon was fractured vs what a Celestine's stated power is and how matter is dependent on spirit rather than the other way around, especially in the case of Celestines, who are said to be able to reconstitute and recover their domain if it's destroyed in the physical world. The only reason that Rorg's patron Celestine and planet bit the dust is because it was a spirit that did that, rather than a purely physical catastrophe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T16:32:32-07:00","id":1088898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1088838#post1088838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i'm fairly certain that the Great Serpent of Pangaea represents one of the few pre-corruption Wyrm manifestations in all of existence, rather than being a closer link to Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Uktena---as in the Uktena tribal Incarna---the same way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T16:39:53-07:00","id":1088901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1088898#post1088898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't Uktena---as in the Uktena tribal Incarna---the same way?</div> </div> </div> </div>More like how Bat operated before going batshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T20:36:07-07:00","id":1088986,"title":"","content":"The Serpent of Pangea seems Gaian to me, holisticly incorporating Serpent myths yeah I can see it representing all of the Triat and thus Primordial Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T06:55:13-07:00","id":1090274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1088838#post1088838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i'm fairly certain that the Great Serpent of Pangaea represents one of the few pre-corruption Wyrm manifestations in all of existence, rather than being a closer link to Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if there is no contradiction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12954-adrax","name":"Adrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T07:38:14-07:00","id":1090299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1090274#post1090274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if there is no contradiction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things don't strike me as that open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:04:55-07:00","id":1091131,"title":"","content":"That's like an individual bacteria trying to speak with it's creator scientist. Even if it could, what would be the point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:06:00-07:00","id":1091240,"title":"","content":"My view is Gaia is a Celestine.<br /> <br /> So, no, you will never, ever be able to meet with her.<br /> <br /> Your TOTEM might talk to Gaia for you. That's, literally, one of their jobs or at least so they claim.<br /> <br /> Spirits, however, lie.<br /> <br /> Many garou in my games have TRIED to talk to Gaia but it's a &quot;Holy Grail quest&quot; which often ends up getting them killed or disgraced. The successes are also very questionable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T06:42:16-07:00","id":1091509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1091240#post1091240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view is Gaia is a Celestine.<br /> <br /> So, no, you will never, ever be able to meet with her.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's objectively wrong given the material's word on the subject. And you can definitely meet Celestine Avatars, but Gaia's avatar is far more scarce than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your TOTEM might talk to Gaia for you. That's, literally, one of their jobs or at least so they claim.<br /> <br /> Spirits, however, lie. </div> </div> </div>Only if it's in their nature to do so. Given the value of the Honor Renown category, I'm guessing they prefer to truck with spirits who don't have such natures, with a few notable exceptions, such as Shadow Lords.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Many garou in my games have TRIED to talk to Gaia but it's a &quot;Holy Grail quest&quot; which often ends up getting them killed or disgraced. The successes are also very questionable. </div> </div> </div>Great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T09:39:06-07:00","id":1091582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1091509#post1091509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's objectively wrong given the material's word on the subject. And you can definitely meet Celestine Avatars, but Gaia's avatar is far more scarce than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Celestine's avatar is for all intents an Incarnae. Why they retconned Under a Blood Red Moon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only if it's in their nature to do so. Given the value of the Honor Renown category, I'm guessing they prefer to truck with spirits who don't have such natures, with a few notable exceptions, such as Shadow Lords. </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure about that because every spirit's nature overrides anything else. A Spirit of Wisdom may appear as Coyote, Odin, or Einstein but will still be spouting things in terms mortals can comprehend.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T10:23:18-07:00","id":1091610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1091582#post1091582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Celestine's avatar is for all intents an Incarnae.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Gaia is above Celestine status. So says the core book. If you read otherwise somewhere, it's probably because the older books didn't have the benefit of errata submission threads and hundreds of eyes on them. There were several instances across various W20 books where someone forgot that Luna was a Celestine and called her an Incarna, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why they retconned Under a Blood Red Moon. </div> </div> </div>Well, they should, at least for its terrible excuse for crossover &quot;guidelines&quot;, but I don't know what you're getting at here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not so sure about that because every spirit's nature overrides anything else. </div> </div> </div>That's the entire idea behind spirits - they are a living, essential nature of something, and cannot freely act against that. The entire idea behind Werewolf, meanwhile, is that you are earnestly struggling toward a worthwhile goal, not that there's a giant conspiracy above your head and that the elders are lying to you. That's Vampire's corner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Spirit of Wisdom may appear as Coyote </div> </div> </div>If we're going by Renown categories, Coyote is Cunning, not Wisdom. Wisdom involves more honest sharing than Cunning implies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Odin </div> </div> </div>Why? So the Fenrir can rip the hapless spirit apart in effigy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or Einstein but will still be spouting things in terms mortals can comprehend. </div> </div> </div>In a language that mortal beings can't. That's why you need Spirit Speech to talk to most spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T01:52:15-07:00","id":1091871,"title":"","content":"Well Gaia's status is still debateable, she certainly doesn't seem to be an ordinary Celestine, but Bastet for instance believe her not to be above the Triat.<br /> <br /> Also some spirits can speak mortal languages, so if a spirit specifically is in the form of Einstein I am guessing he will probably be speaking like English or German, or some other human language associated with the pop image of Einstein.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T01:55:01-07:00","id":1091872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1091871#post1091871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Gaia's status is still debateable, she certainly doesn't seem to be an ordinary Celestine, but Bastet for instance believe her not to be above the Triat.<br /> <br /> Also some spirits can speak mortal languages, so if a spirit specifically is in the form of Einstein I am guessing he will probably be speaking like English or German, or some other human language associated with the pop image of Einstein.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, I think Garou should actually have elevated her beyond her station in their pantheon and the Triat should be above her.<br /> <br /> Because the Garou are, kind of arrogant blowhards about everything.<br /> <br /> It's why we love them.<br /> <br /> In other words, I wouldn't be surprised if Gaia is Eshtarra and the Garou just pretend otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T07:27:33-07:00","id":1091937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1091872#post1091872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Generally, I think Garou should actually have elevated her beyond her station in their pantheon and the Triat should be above her.</div> </div> </div> </div>A possibility fielded by the core book, but one which the material following the core book doesn't play ball with in the slightest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because the Garou are, kind of arrogant blowhards about everything.<br /> <br /> It's why we love them.<br /> <br /> In other words, I wouldn't be surprised if Gaia is Eshtarra and the Garou just pretend otherwise. </div> </div> </div>That would be a major-league Vampire kind of move. Problem: this game is not Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T09:05:23-07:00","id":1091973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1091937#post1091937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be a major-league Vampire kind of move. Problem: this game is not Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>No because Garou believe their own lies. It's why the War of Rage was justified and hitting every problem will eventually solve it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T11:48:45-07:00","id":1092021,"title":"","content":"So you defend this statement:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1091973#post1091973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I wouldn't be surprised if Gaia is Eshtarra and the Garou just pretend otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>With-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1091973#post1091973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Garou believe their own lies. It's why the War of Rage was justified and hitting every problem will eventually solve it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing in the source material to assume that because the Garou are arrogant, they can ignore/reinvent how the spirit world works. Furthermore, other changing breeds, even the ones slaughtered by the Garou, seem to be laboring under the impression they are serving Gaia also. That doesn't really jive if Gaia is just an Incarna designed to be worshiped by the Garou.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to play up a cosmological conspiracy angle, go for it, but I don't think it makes a lick of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T12:39:17-07:00","id":1092052,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's what CTPhipps is saying. I interpret his words to mean that since there is a lot about the spirit world that Garou and everyone else simply don't know, that the Garou have naturally filled in the gaps with what they think is the truth. Whether or not that is actually the truth isn't really knowable, or at least not verifiable. But since it is Garou dogma, they believe it completely with no doubt. Someone else from a different perspective, would come to a different conclusion or hold off from any conclusion. They have just as much evidence for their beliefs as the Garou does theirs, but no Garou would ever admit it. It's not a conspiracy at all - it's just blind faith and dogma.<br /> <br /> I think this holds more true for the idea that Gaia is &quot;just&quot; a Celestine rather than above the Triat, rather than the Eshtarra Incarna. However, even at the level of Incarna, it's gotten way past the point people can really speak to certainty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T13:34:42-07:00","id":1092080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1092052#post1092052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's what CTPhipps is saying. I interpret his words to mean that since there is a lot about the spirit world that Garou and everyone else simply don't know, that the Garou have naturally filled in the gaps with what they think is the truth. Whether or not that is actually the truth isn't really knowable, or at least not verifiable. But since it is Garou dogma, they believe it completely with no doubt. Someone else from a different perspective, would come to a different conclusion or hold off from any conclusion. They have just as much evidence for their beliefs as the Garou does theirs, but no Garou would ever admit it. It's not a conspiracy at all - it's just blind faith and dogma.<br /> <br /> I think this holds more true for the idea that Gaia is &quot;just&quot; a Celestine rather than above the Triat, rather than the Eshtarra Incarna. However, even at the level of Incarna, it's gotten way past the point people can really speak to certainty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incarnae can hold discourse with lesser beings. Higher than that, and things get difficult.<br /> <br /> That said, this still isn't a game about cosmological conspiracy theories, and metatextually speaking, you should be able to fill in any gaps as an author to shut out room for cosmological conspiracy theories to take root. It's neither here nor there, and if you go off the rails to include cosmological conspiracy theories, then you're on your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T14:05:12-07:00","id":1092094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1092021#post1092021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is nothing in the source material to assume that because the Garou are arrogant, they can ignore/reinvent how the spirit world works. Furthermore, other changing breeds, even the ones slaughtered by the Garou, seem to be laboring under the impression they are serving Gaia also. That doesn't really jive if Gaia is just an Incarna designed to be worshiped by the Garou.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to play up a cosmological conspiracy angle, go for it, but I don't think it makes a lick of sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot to unpack there but you basically seem to be thinking I'm imagining a bunch of Garou Cardinals, sitting around the Vatican in Red Robes doing Davinchi Code stuff. No, I'm not. First of all, in this interpretation of canon, it's not Gaia as an Incarnae. If she was an Incarnae the Garou could journey to her realm and talk to her the same way I could go talk to the President. It would be extremely difficult, possibly get me killed, but it's not difficult. I suggested Gaia is a CELESTINE which is magnitudes more difficult to communicate with and more powerful. I do think Eshtarra is an AVATAR of Gaia but that means Gaia is so potent that even her lesser form is mind-boggling powerful. Less the President and getting a meeting with God. I might go to a sweathouse, take hallucinogens, or pray for months to get a vision from him but I'm not going to stand in front of him unless there's something miraculous happening.<br /> <br /> However, my argument is the Garou have raised Gaia the Celestine up to a Judeao-Christian God-Above-All ideal above all the others when I don't think that actually tracks with what we know about the cosmology. No, Gaia should be the most important Celestine to Garou and Homids because we live on her, not because she's the most powerful or above the others.<br /> <br /> I also enjoy poking holes in Garou fundamentalism given how much the books contradict one another, the tribes have differing legends, and it's clear so very much of what we know about the Umbra is filtered through Garou prejudices.<br /> <br /> And yes, shifters in general.<br /> <br /> Or, to REALLY cut it down to its bare minimum, I think the Spirit World probably works like Exalted more than it does the Garou model. It's just there's no Exalted or Celestial Bureaucracy. Gaia is just one of many Celestines, not the head honcho and less powerful than the Wyrm, Weaver, or Wyld. Not that Sol, Jupiter, or Mars are all that interested in our situation.<br /> <br /> Incarnae can hold discourse with lesser beings. Higher than that, and things get difficult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, this still isn't a game about cosmological conspiracy theories, and metatextually speaking, you should be able to fill in any gaps as an author to shut out room for cosmological conspiracy theories to take root. It's neither here nor there, and if you go off the rails to include cosmological conspiracy theories, then you're on your own. </div> </div> </div>I think W:TA is a game about MYTHOLOGY and to a lesser extent religion in general. A lot of the game is about three things:<br /> <br /> 1. The history of the Garou<br /> 2. How the Garou interpret that history<br /> 3. How reality was<br /> <br /> It's also reflected in the Spirit World as we constantly have stories of how the Weaver, Wyrm, Wyld, and other myths are true or not. Did the Weaver corrupt the Wyrm? Is the Wyrm the real enemy? Much of the Garou history is told in stories which make the game very subjective. I think as mythology, exploring what's true or not is a very big theme of the game if you're interested in its theology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-13-2017, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T14:55:07-07:00","id":1092109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1092094#post1092094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a lot to unpack there but you basically seem to be thinking I'm imagining a bunch of Garou Cardinals, sitting around the Vatican in Red Robes doing Davinchi Code stuff. No, I'm not. First of all, in this interpretation of canon, it's not Gaia as an Incarnae. If she was an Incarnae the Garou could journey to her realm and talk to her the same way I could go talk to the President. It would be extremely difficult, possibly get me killed, but it's not difficult. I suggested Gaia is a CELESTINE which is magnitudes more difficult to communicate with and more powerful. I do think Eshtarra is an AVATAR of Gaia but that means Gaia is so potent that even her lesser form is mind-boggling powerful. Less the President and getting a meeting with God. I might go to a sweathouse, take hallucinogens, or pray for months to get a vision from him but I'm not going to stand in front of him unless there's something miraculous happening.<br /> <br /> However, my argument is the Garou have raised Gaia the Celestine up to a Judeao-Christian God-Above-All ideal above all the others when I don't think that actually tracks with what we know about the cosmology. No, Gaia should be the most important Celestine to Garou and Homids because we live on her, not because she's the most powerful or above the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what? I mean, homids weren't the predominant breed for most of Garou history, but that aside, think about what the game's lore was set up for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also enjoy poking holes in Garou fundamentalism given how much the books contradict one another, the tribes have differing legends, and it's clear so very much of what we know about the Umbra is filtered through Garou prejudices.<br /> <br /> And yes, shifters in general.<br /> <br /> Or, to REALLY cut it down to its bare minimum, I think the Spirit World probably works like Exalted more than it does the Garou model. It's just there's no Exalted or Celestial Bureaucracy. Gaia is just one of many Celestines, not the head honcho and less powerful than the Wyrm, Weaver, or Wyld. Not that Sol, Jupiter, or Mars are all that interested in our situation. </div> </div> </div>No, Exalted is the demonstrable opposite of how Werewolf works in many cases, and it certainly isn't anywhere near close. Case in Point 1, Exalted's gods are just bureaucrats, where as spirits in Werewolf are the living Essence of something, and that something cannot survive the death of the spirit. Case in Point 2, the spiritual ranking in Exalted isn't the same; Point 3, Gaia is a completely different being, a Primordial rather than a god; Point 4, any direct connection between the WoD and Exalted were severed before the first edition core of Exalted hit the shelves, as described in the first edition Exalted Storyteller's Companion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think W:TA is a game about MYTHOLOGY and to a lesser extent religion in general. A lot of the game is about three things:<br /> <br /> 1. The history of the Garou<br /> 2. How the Garou interpret that history<br /> 3. How reality was<br /> <br /> It's also reflected in the Spirit World as we constantly have stories of how the Weaver, Wyrm, Wyld, and other myths are true or not. Did the Weaver corrupt the Wyrm? Is the Wyrm the real enemy? Much of the Garou history is told in stories which make the game very subjective. I think as mythology, exploring what's true or not is a very big theme of the game if you're interested in its theology. </div> </div> </div>If there's one thing that Werewolf emphatically isn't about, that would be subjectivity. The Weaver did ensnare the Wyrm... but that doesn't change the fact that all the bits and pieces of the Wyrm are trying to keep it that way, so for all intents and purposes, no member of the Triat is actually an ally of anything more than convenience, not even the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Religion comes into Werewolf in the form of an approach to rites that they practice. The existence of spirits as laid down in the core book? Not up for negotiation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T15:03:24-07:00","id":1092112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If there's one thing that Werewolf emphatically isn't about, that would be subjectivity. </div> </div> </div>Wow...just...<br /> <br /> What now?<br /> <br /> Werewolf is ALL about subjectivity. Not a single tribe agrees about ANYTHING other than Gaia Good, Wyrm Evil and even then not always that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T15:28:52-07:00","id":1092117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1092112#post1092112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow...just...<br /> <br /> What now?<br /> <br /> Werewolf is ALL about subjectivity. Not a single tribe agrees about ANYTHING other than Gaia Good, Wyrm Evil and even then not always that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the subjectivity we're talking about, here, because it takes the form of nuance rather than pulling the fucking rug out from under everything. Also, it's definitely the case that Gaia is worth fighting for, and this is another thing not up for debate. Central theme of the game, if you don't like it, you have a lot of modding to do, and might be better off looking for another game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T16:29:12-07:00","id":1092142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1092117#post1092117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not the subjectivity we're talking about, here, because it takes the form of nuance rather than pulling the fucking rug out from under everything. Also, it's definitely the case that Gaia is worth fighting for, and this is another thing not up for debate. Central theme of the game, if you don't like it, you have a lot of modding to do, and might be better off looking for another game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't she be worth fighting for?<br /> <br /> Earth is where the Garou keep their stuff.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying the rest of the galaxy wouldn't care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T19:36:10-07:00","id":1092188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1092142#post1092142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why wouldn't she be worth fighting for?<br /> <br /> Earth is where the Garou keep their stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's grand scale missing the point. Humans think that the Earth is where they keep their stuff. Garou feel more as a part of the spiritual world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm just saying the rest of the galaxy wouldn't care. </div> </div> </div>Also not true. The Aetherial Realm connects space far more expediently than the physical world, allowing for sweeps of distant stars far, far faster than physics would allow. The needs of the campaign setting, however, have it that there are no distant stars to which to flee. The wars on Earth decide far more than what happens on Earth, or in the physical world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T19:54:23-07:00","id":1092196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1092188#post1092188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's grand scale missing the point. Humans think that the Earth is where they keep their stuff. Garou feel more as a part of the spiritual world.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is manifestly not true. If Gaia goes, the Garou go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also not true. The Aetherial Realm connects space far more expediently than the physical world, allowing for sweeps of distant stars far, far faster than physics would allow. The needs of the campaign setting, however, have it that there are no distant stars to which to flee. The wars on Earth decide far more than what happens on Earth, or in the physical world. </div> </div> </div>If Gaia dies, Helios will be fine.<br /> <br /> Not that any Garou would flee Gaia, that would get you killed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T21:01:02-07:00","id":1092214,"title":"","content":"Gaia isn't just 'the earth.' Gaia is all of Creation, above Helios, Luna, or the Triat.<br /> <br /> If Gaia 'dies' (whatever that means), it's game over man, for the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T22:04:38-07:00","id":1092232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1092214#post1092214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaia isn't just 'the earth.' Gaia is all of Creation, above Helios, Luna, or the Triat.<br /> <br /> If Gaia 'dies' (whatever that means), it's game over man, for the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I never liked that and it doesn't feel appropriate for the setting, IMHO.<br /> <br /> But there are book quotes to approve it.<br /> <br /> Personally, it strikes me as something the Garou would make up to make themselves feel more important.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T08:30:51-07:00","id":1092336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1092232#post1092232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I never liked that and it doesn't feel appropriate for the setting, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your opinion doesn't seem very humble at the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But there are book quotes to approve it.<br /> <br /> Personally, it strikes me as something the Garou would make up to make themselves feel more important. </div> </div> </div>Except that the Corax and the Nuwisha would back them up on it from the body of their own experiences on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:52:43-07:00","id":1092438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1091871#post1091871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Gaia's status is still debateable, she certainly doesn't seem to be an ordinary Celestine, but Bastet for instance believe her not to be above the Triat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. If I remember correctly, the Ananasi also put forth the belief that Gaia is created by (and therefore not above) the Triat. I love the ambiguity.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as a more general response to the thread: That Gaia as well as the Triat are not personified directly in a way that's meaningful to the changing breeds is awesome. To me, it's more like these things are the foundation concepts that make up existence rather than a thing with a specific, embodied mind (spirit or otherwise--I'm using &quot;embodied&quot; lightly here, 'cause it's hard for me to find the words to put a nebulous concept into a form). How can the Wyrm ever be destroyed, for example, if it's not a single entity? How can the Weaver be reasoned with directly to ease up her own mad reactions, with the same point of view? That's why avatars are even needed; you don't need to create a singular form to interact with things if you're already a singular form that can interact with things.<br /> <br /> I don't think there is a straightforward &quot;these are the facts&quot; explanation about the Triat and about Gaia, including who created whom. The text (outside of the hard rules themselves) in Werewolf Core is very, well, Storytelling. Same with the text for the rest of the Fera. It seems to me to be written from their point of view, which will naturally contain their bias. If it's all 100% true, there are some pretty big consistency issues which damage the experience of the world. If, instead, it's viewed as bias information, filling in the gaps of what they don't know with speculation that is taken as true by those who follow a particular creed (especially all this time later in their history), it makes the world that much more rich and intriguing.<br /> <br /> I realize that I've used language that promotes certain things as fact; please understand I don't mean it that way, but as my view on the subject. Considering I see the concepts of Gaia and the Triat as somewhat unfathomable, in that every definition of them will naturally always fall short of what and who they really are, I hope that makes sense. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, that's how I understand and interact with the material. Obviously it's not the only way to take it. If playing in another campaign with a Storyteller who sees it differently, I defer to their interpretation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T15:25:18-07:00","id":1092537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1092336#post1092336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that the Corax and the Nuwisha would back them up on it from the body of their own experiences on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem being that other Shifters disagree like the Bastet and Anasasi disagree.<br /> <br /> Notable fact: Both Corax and Nuwisha are also the two shifters closest to the Garou.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T18:29:10-07:00","id":1092602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1088272-how-to-talk-with-gaia?p=1092537#post1092537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem being that other Shifters disagree like the Bastet and Anasasi disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>The former value Cunning over Wisdom and are notoriously unwilling to give out secrets to others. The latter actually have a Trait to measure how unthinkingly obedient they are to someone feeding them an &quot;all you need to know&quot; style of information and are also extremely hesitant or completely unwilling to share secrets. If the BS line is coming from anywhere, it'd be them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Notable fact: Both Corax and Nuwisha are also the two shifters closest to the Garou. </div> </div> </div>The Nuwisha not really so much. They hide among them and pretend to be them, but are also constantly testing the Garou and you can't really say that they get along. That is, the ones still on Earth do this. The rest are off among the Deep Umbra and the reaches of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> As for the Corax, they have to deliver information as accurate as possible to as many people as they can. It's basically etched into the core of their being and upheld by their society's ideals - they can't shut their yaps, and they value the truth. They're close to all of the other Fera as a result, though they also irritate them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}